<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal parliament okays general '97 budget terms.</title>
<headline>Portugal parliament okays general '97 budget terms.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal's parliament on Friday approved, in a vote, the general terms of the Socialist government's 1997 budget proposals, parliamentary speaker Antonio Almeida Santos said.</p>
<p>The ruling Socialists voted in favour of the budget, the main opposition centre-right Social Democratic Party (PSD) abstained and the smaller rightwing Popular Party (PP), Communist Party (PCP) and Green Party voted against.</p>
</text>
